Task: classify 250 bp bacterial DNA reads as from pathogenic or nonpathogenic genomes (labels at organism level).
Train/val/test are genome-disjoint. 6-mer words more frequent per genome in each class (replicated on held-out genomes):
{"more_in_pathogenic": ["GCTAGC", "AACCCT", "AGGGTT", "AACCCA", "CTAGCG", "CGCTAG", "GCACTA", "TAGTGC", "TGGGTT", "GGCTAG", "CTAGCC", "GCTAGG", "CCTAGC", "GCTCTA", "TAGAGC", "GGTTAG", "CTAGCT", "CCCTAG", "AGCTAG", "TCTAGC"], "more_in_nonpathogenic": ["CATGGA", "TGTTCC", "GGATAC", "GTATCC", "TCCATG", "ATGTCC", "GGAACA", "GGACAT", "ACGGAA", "ATACGG", "TTCCGT", "CGGAAT", "ATCCGT", "TCCGAT", "TACGGA", "ATTCCG", "TTCCGA", "TCCGGA", "CCGTAT", "ACGGAT"]}
GC content separates the classes weakly: genome-level AUC of GC = 0.45 (train), 0.41 (held out).
Word-effect direction agreement train->held-out genomes: 100% for the top 6-mers.
Reverse-complement test: embeddings do not treat a word and its reverse complement as similar (word2vec cosine 0.19 vs 0.17 random).
Model AUCs (read-level, and genome-level via mean read score) on validation and test only. Other evaluation sets (truncated reads, letter-shuffled reads, a different curated database) are hidden from you on purpose; Q3 and Q4 ask you to predict them:
cnn: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.881, "genome_auc": 0.904}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.793, "genome_auc": 0.868}}
mlp: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.895, "genome_auc": 0.923}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.774, "genome_auc": 0.829}}
gru: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.894, "genome_auc": 0.932}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.782, "genome_auc": 0.838}}
transformer: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.855, "genome_auc": 0.868}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.778, "genome_auc": 0.859}}
dnabert2: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.89, "genome_auc": 0.88}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.781, "genome_auc": 0.838}}
dnabert2_scratch: {"test_pooled": {"read_auc": 0.501, "genome_auc": 0.786}, "val": {"read_auc": 0.501, "genome_auc": 0.564}}

